  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Conformal Mappings [S+N]\n\nA holomorphic function $f$ with $f'(z_0) \\ne 0$ is **conformal** at $z_0$: it preserves angles. The proof is one line — the differential is multiplication by $f'(z_0)$, and complex multiplication is rotation + scaling, both of which preserve angles.\n\nThis is the *geometric* face of holomorphy. Beyond preserving angles, there are deep theorems:\n\n- **Open mapping theorem**: a non-constant holomorphic function takes open sets to open sets.\n- **Schwarz lemma**: holomorphic $f : \\mathbb{D} \\to \\mathbb{D}$ with $f(0) = 0$ satisfies $|f(z)| \\le |z|$.\n- **Riemann mapping theorem**: every simply connected proper open subset of $\\mathbb{C}$ is conformally equivalent to the unit disk.\n\nThis notebook visualises the angle-preservation, walks the disc automorphisms, and ends with a glimpse of the Riemann mapping theorem.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Angle preservation visualised\n\nMap the orthogonal grid of horizontal and vertical lines under $f(z) = z^2$. Where the grid lines cross at right angles in the input, the images cross at right angles in the output — except at the origin, where $f'(0) = 0$ and conformality fails.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Plot horizontal lines y = const and vertical lines x = const, then their images under z² */\nn_show : 5$\nn_pts : 100$\nys_const : [0.4, 0.7, 1.0, 1.3]$\nxs_const : [0.4, 0.7, 1.0, 1.3]$\n\n/* Image of horizontal line y = c: z = x + ic, z² = (x²-c²) + i(2xc) */\nbuild_h_image(c) := block([xs, re_im, im_im],\n  xs : np_to_list(np_linspace(-1.5, 1.5, n_pts)),\n  re_im : map(lambda([xx], xx*xx - c*c), xs),\n  im_im : map(lambda([xx], 2*xx*c), xs),\n  [re_im, im_im])$\nbuild_v_image(c) := block([ys, re_im, im_im],\n  ys : np_to_list(np_linspace(-1.5, 1.5, n_pts)),\n  re_im : map(lambda([yy], c*c - yy*yy), ys),\n  im_im : map(lambda([yy], 2*c*yy), ys),\n  [re_im, im_im])$\n\nh1 : build_h_image(0.4)$  h2 : build_h_image(0.8)$  h3 : build_h_image(1.2)$\nv1 : build_v_image(0.4)$  v2 : build_v_image(0.8)$  v3 : build_v_image(1.2)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"image of horizontals\",\n  lines(h1[1], h1[2]),\n  color=\"blue\",\n  lines(h2[1], h2[2]),\n  color=\"blue\",\n  lines(h3[1], h3[2]),\n  color=\"red\", line_width=2, name=\"image of verticals\",\n  lines(v1[1], v1[2]),\n  color=\"red\",\n  lines(v2[1], v2[2]),\n  color=\"red\",\n  lines(v3[1], v3[2]),\n  title=\"Image of orthogonal grid under z² — angles preserved (parabolas meet at right angles)\",\n  xlabel=\"Re\", ylabel=\"Im\",\n  grid=true, aspect_ratio=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
